24
00:01:00,410 --> 00:01:01,810
The official definition is...

25
00:01:01,810 --> 00:01:05,890
It turns project work into a set of isolated, self-contained tasks.

26
00:01:05,890 --> 00:01:06,820
execution.

27
00:01:06,820 --> 00:01:09,220
Now, pay attention to three key words: isolated,

28
00:01:09,220 --> 00:01:10,960
and autonomous execution.

29
00:01:10,960 --> 00:01:12,280
These three words are key.

30
00:01:12,280 --> 00:01:14,180
Symphony isn't a tool for writing code.

31
00:01:14,180 --> 00:01:15,620
but rather, a scheduler.

32
00:01:15,620 --> 00:01:18,430
So, here's how it works.

33
00:01:18,430 --> 00:01:20,030
on your Linear board,

34
00:01:20,030 --> 00:01:22,580
Symphony will check on every single ticket.

35
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:25,500
and is in a 'to do' or 'in progress' state,

36
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:27,620
and there are no unresolved blockers.

37
00:01:27,620 --> 00:01:30,090
it will then dispatch an agent to get it done.

38
00:01:30,090 --> 00:01:34,160
This agent runs in its own dedicated workspace.

39
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:37,620
The agent itself runs on OpenAI's Codex observer.

40
00:01:37,620 --> 00:01:40,070
Symphony itself is only responsible for scheduling.

41
00:01:40,070 --> 00:01:41,710
Who should run it, and for how long?

42
00:01:41,710 --> 00:01:43,210
What happens if it times out?

43
00:01:43,210 --> 00:01:44,850
